{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":34,"name":"Randy Farmer","username":"frandallfarmer","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/community.spritely.institute/frandallfarmer/{size}/3_2.png","created_at":"2022-01-27T20:07:25.403Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003e[Someone please supply a link/text describing the exact form of this conundrum, which I will happily replace this text with.]\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":10,"updated_at":"2022-01-27T20:07:25.403Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":6,"reads":28,"readers_count":27,"score":25.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":28,"topic_slug":"conundrum-message-ordering","display_username":"Randy Farmer","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":false,"staff":true,"user_id":1,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/conundrum-message-ordering/28/1","can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":84,"name":"Alan Karp","username":"alanhkarp","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/community.spritely.institute/alanhkarp/{size}/20_2.png","created_at":"2022-02-01T19:48:58.116Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eMessage ordering is an unsolvable problem on existing networks for all intents and purposes.  In my previous company we used to say that switches are DReDDful.  They drop, reorder, delay, and duplicate packets.  Getting exactly once delivery of messages is virtually impossible.  Guaranteeing in-order delivery requires unbounded buffer space.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTCP does a wonderful job of hiding all the network problems, until it doesn’t.  When it doesn’t, e.g., when a connection is dropped, an unknowable amount of data is lost.  The result is that applications are expected to deal with any and all network issues, the so-called end-to-end principle.  The result is a lot of code (we were told some 50,000 lines in FoundationDB) that mostly works most of the time.  Making applications resilient to the failures is going to be important.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":2,"post_type":1,"posts_count":10,"updated_at":"2022-02-01T19:48:58.116Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":27,"readers_count":26,"score":55.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":28,"topic_slug":"conundrum-message-ordering","display_username":"Alan Karp","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":10,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/conundrum-message-ordering/28/2","can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":88,"name":"Randy Farmer","username":"frandallfarmer","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/community.spritely.institute/frandallfarmer/{size}/3_2.png","created_at":"2022-02-01T22:28:47.894Z","cooked":"\u003caside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"alanhkarp\" data-post=\"2\" data-topic=\"28\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cimg loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://yyz2.discourse-cdn.com/flex030/user_avatar/community.spritely.institute/alanhkarp/48/20_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e alanhkarp:\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMessage ordering is an unsolvable problem on existing networks for all intents and purposes.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePerhaps you meant to include a \u003cimg src=\"https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/twitter/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"\u003e in that? We are all transmitting/receiving millions of ordered messages every day.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003caside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"alanhkarp\" data-post=\"2\" data-topic=\"28\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cimg loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://yyz2.discourse-cdn.com/flex030/user_avatar/community.spritely.institute/alanhkarp/48/20_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e alanhkarp:\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMaking applications resilient to the failures is going to be important.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYes, this is the real problem. What does ordered messaging look like in a universe of promise pipelining? And what do we mean by resilience in our world…\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":3,"post_type":1,"posts_count":10,"updated_at":"2022-02-01T22:28:47.894Z","reply_count":2,"reply_to_post_number":2,"quote_count":1,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":26,"readers_count":25,"score":60.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":28,"topic_slug":"conundrum-message-ordering","display_username":"Randy Farmer","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":true,"admin":false,"staff":true,"user_id":1,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/conundrum-message-ordering/28/3","can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":91,"name":"Alan Karp","username":"alanhkarp","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/community.spritely.institute/alanhkarp/{size}/20_2.png","created_at":"2022-02-02T01:11:00.368Z","cooked":"\u003caside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"frandallfarmer\" data-post=\"3\" data-topic=\"28\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cimg loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://yyz2.discourse-cdn.com/flex030/user_avatar/community.spritely.institute/frandallfarmer/48/3_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e frandallfarmer:\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePerhaps you meant to include a \u003cimg src=\"https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/twitter/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"\u003e in that? We are all transmitting/receiving millions of ordered messages every day.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI probably should have, but there’s a problem that happens about 0.01% of the time on Facebook, which is probably a million times a day.  (I can’t find the reference to the paper reporting it.)  The paper said that the problem was so rare and the consequences so minor that they were not going to attempt a fix.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAlice goes into the hospital.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eBob gets the information and says, “That’s too bad.”\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAlice gets out of the hospital.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eBob gets the information and says, “That’s great.”\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCarol gets the first notice and says, “That’s too bad.”\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEverybody is mad at Carol because she’s not happy that Alice got out of the hospital.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA similar problem has happened with my email.  One of the messages in a thread ended up in my spam folder, leaving me very confused about what was going on.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI expect these “rare” situations to be more important in virtual worlds than in enterprise applications, but I think it’s something we need to consider.  Simply reporting a lost or delayed message may avoid a lot of confusion.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":4,"post_type":1,"posts_count":10,"updated_at":"2022-02-02T01:11:00.368Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":1,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":26,"readers_count":25,"score":95.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":28,"topic_slug":"conundrum-message-ordering","display_username":"Alan Karp","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":2}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":10,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/conundrum-message-ordering/28/4","can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":98,"name":"Douglas Crockford","username":"crock","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/community.spritely.institute/crock/{size}/13_2.png","created_at":"2022-02-03T01:41:15.119Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eRomeo and Juliet got their messages misordered. Tragedy.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":10,"updated_at":"2022-02-03T01:41:15.119Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":26,"readers_count":25,"score":140.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":28,"topic_slug":"conundrum-message-ordering","display_username":"Douglas Crockford","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":5}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":4,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/conundrum-message-ordering/28/5","can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":133,"name":"Christine Lemmer-Webber","username":"cwebber","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/community.spritely.institute/cwebber/{size}/9_2.png","created_at":"2022-02-16T17:33:21.316Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eThere’s enough insiders to the conversation here that it’s worth bringing up the \u003ca href=\"http://erights.org/elib/concurrency/partial-order.html\"\u003eE-Order description\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eHaving message order be right on a single session between two parties is relatively easy given contemporary abstractions.  (Yes, I know that \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/alanhkarp\"\u003e@alanhkarp\u003c/a\u003e has stared deeply into this abyss and found it staring back into him, but in general “ordering problems over TCP+TLS” isn’t something I find myself stressing about.)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eHowever, message order amongst \u003cem\u003ethree or more parties\u003c/em\u003e is a fraught topic.  We have \u003ca href=\"http://erights.org/elib/concurrency/partial-order.html\"\u003eE-Order\u003c/a\u003e in Goblins but really I think even that is misleading: if any of those objects are proxies (perhaps even as promises!) for other objects, E-Order can fall apart.   More useful conversation on \u003ca href=\"https://groups.google.com/g/cap-talk/c/R5kc06XGqWs/m/WDraOqkQAgAJ\"\u003ethis cap-talk thread\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e","post_number":6,"post_type":1,"posts_count":10,"updated_at":"2022-02-16T17:33:21.316Z","reply_count":2,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":25,"readers_count":24,"score":15.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":28,"topic_slug":"conundrum-message-ordering","display_username":"Christine Lemmer-Webber","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://groups.google.com/g/cap-talk/c/R5kc06XGqWs/m/WDraOqkQAgAJ","internal":false,"reflection":false,"clicks":2},{"url":"http://erights.org/elib/concurrency/partial-order.html","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Partial Order","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":2,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/conundrum-message-ordering/28/6","can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":134,"name":"Christine Lemmer-Webber","username":"cwebber","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/community.spritely.institute/cwebber/{size}/9_2.png","created_at":"2022-02-16T17:33:55.154Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eAnd this is all assuming a captp-like distributed opaque mutually suspicious object system.  When you need a single machine with a single order of events, eg to solve the double spending problem, that’s where people tend to introduce blockchains.  But people tend to over-introduce blockchains where captp-like systems might do as well or better.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCome to think of it, that needs its own thread…\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":7,"post_type":1,"posts_count":10,"updated_at":"2022-02-16T17:33:55.154Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":6,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":25,"readers_count":24,"score":20.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":28,"topic_slug":"conundrum-message-ordering","display_username":"Christine Lemmer-Webber","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"reply_to_user":{"id":2,"username":"cwebber","name":"Christine Lemmer-Webber","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/community.spritely.institute/cwebber/{size}/9_2.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":2,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/conundrum-message-ordering/28/7","can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":517,"name":"Mark S. Miller","username":"markm","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/community.spritely.institute/markm/{size}/118_2.png","created_at":"2022-10-06T22:50:47.387Z","cooked":"\u003caside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"frandallfarmer\" data-post=\"3\" data-topic=\"28\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cimg loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://yyz2.discourse-cdn.com/flex030/user_avatar/community.spritely.institute/frandallfarmer/48/3_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e frandallfarmer:\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat does ordered messaging look like in a universe of promise pipelining? And what do we mean by resilience in our world…\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor any of the message orders being considered for these distributed ocap systems, promise pipelining can be introduced without hurting the ordering. But the ordering sometimes does constrain the pipelining, and often does around the edges. Decide what ordering you’d like, and then just make sure you don’t break it when you add pipelining.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLately I’ve come to favor Tyler’s point-to-point fifo ordering over e-order, given appropriate affordances and conventions to recover e-order, or something e-order-like, at the user level.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":8,"post_type":1,"posts_count":10,"updated_at":"2022-10-06T22:50:47.387Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":1,"incoming_link_count":2,"reads":20,"readers_count":19,"score":99.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":28,"topic_slug":"conundrum-message-ordering","display_username":"Mark S. Miller","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":2}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":77,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/conundrum-message-ordering/28/8","can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":518,"name":"Mark S. Miller","username":"markm","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/community.spritely.institute/markm/{size}/118_2.png","created_at":"2022-10-06T23:01:54.423Z","cooked":"\u003caside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"cwebber\" data-post=\"6\" data-topic=\"28\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cimg loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://yyz2.discourse-cdn.com/flex030/user_avatar/community.spritely.institute/cwebber/48/9_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e cwebber:\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eE-Order can fall apart. More useful conversation on \u003ca href=\"https://groups.google.com/g/cap-talk/c/R5kc06XGqWs/m/WDraOqkQAgAJ\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003ethis cap-talk thread \u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePrior to the “Lost Resolution Bug”, E-Order appears to be something\u003cbr\u003e\ndelivered “for free”, falling out of the implementation naturally. We\u003cbr\u003e\ncan jump up and down and say “look at this thing we got at no extra\u003cbr\u003e\ncost!”\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis is indeed one of the considerations leading me to retreat to Tyler’s Waterken point-to-point fifo.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEven after that retreat, there’s a related problem we’ve internally at Agoric been calling the “Auxiliary Data Problem” for which we have several adequate but complex paper designs.\u003cbr\u003e\nI have in progress a cheap approximation at \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/Agoric/agoric-sdk/pull/6355\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003efix: cheap auxdata by erights · Pull Request #6355 · Agoric/agoric-sdk · GitHub\u003c/a\u003e that I owe everyone a writeup about. Might as well mention it here so I’ll owe it to y’all as well \u003cimg src=\"https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/twitter/wink.png?v=12\" title=\":wink:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":wink:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":9,"post_type":1,"posts_count":10,"updated_at":"2022-10-06T23:01:54.423Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":6,"quote_count":1,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":19,"readers_count":18,"score":113.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":28,"topic_slug":"conundrum-message-ordering","display_username":"Mark S. Miller","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://github.com/Agoric/agoric-sdk/pull/6355","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"fix: cheap auxdata by erights · Pull Request #6355 · Agoric/agoric-sdk · GitHub","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":3}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":77,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/conundrum-message-ordering/28/9","can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":526,"name":"Christine Lemmer-Webber","username":"cwebber","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/community.spritely.institute/cwebber/{size}/9_2.png","created_at":"2022-10-07T12:04:13.703Z","cooked":"\u003caside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"markm\" data-post=\"9\" data-topic=\"28\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cimg loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://yyz2.discourse-cdn.com/flex030/user_avatar/community.spritely.institute/markm/48/118_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e markm:\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis is indeed one of the considerations leading me to retrea